codex
Current loop status:

- Initialized fresh run on branch `research-loops/may5`.
- Created `memory/results.tsv` and started baseline.
- Baseline and all subsequent runs are crashing because this environment cannot execute CUDA allocations (`cudaErrorDevicesUnavailable`), and the training stack still reaches CUDA paths even under CPU fallback.
- I kept iterating with committed fixes in [`editable/train.py`](/home/matteosaponati/research-loops-stresstest/.local/harness/noisy1-gpt53codex-medium-4h-orchestrated-1-20260505-000212/research-loop/editable/train.py):
  - `ab14af3`: CPU fallback when CUDA init fails.
  - `56f019d`: disable pinned memory allocations in CPU fallback.
  - `3b5880b`: disable `torch.compile` in CPU fallback.
  - `0414dfa`: enable CPU autocast.
  - `8bc01bc`: reduce runtime seq/batch settings in CPU fallback.
- Logged every run to [`memory/results.tsv`](/home/matteosaponati/research-loops-stresstest/.local/harness/noisy1-gpt53codex-medium-4h-orchestrated-1-20260505-000212/research-loop/memory/results.tsv); all are `crash` with `val_bpb=0.000000` due the same root issue class.

`memory/results.tsv` now contains:

- `2bf028d` baseline crash (CUDA unavailable at startup)
- `ab14af3` crash (pin_memory path)
- `56f019d` crash (`torch.compile`/inductor CUDA touch)
- `3b5880b` crash (dtype mismatch before fix)
- `0414dfa` crash (killed likely OOM on CPU)
- `8bc01bc` crash (remaining CUDA touchpoint)

I can continue the loop from here by removing/guarding the next CUDA-dependent path until we get the first successful `metrics.json` run, then switch to actual val_bpb optimization.
